      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Eagle's syndrome has received scant attention in both medical and dental literature. The symptoms related to this condition can be confused with those attributed to a wide variety of facial neuralgias. The present case refers to a 46-year-old white woman with the symptomatology of Eagle's syndrome, especially the carotid artery type."},
